# The filter table, applied whole by wireguard-hub-up (hub design 3.3). Forwarding is dropped
# unless a flow is listed here; replies to a permitted flow are accepted. One ACCEPT line per flow,
# a spoke's /32 to a peer's /32 on named ports. INPUT is not touched: Docker publishes the UDP port
# and the container's default INPUT policy accepts.
*filter
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:FORWARD DROP [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT
# camera-footage-fs (public ingress) to cffs-pc's SFTPGo: SFTP and the web client only.
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.23/32 -d 10.8.0.22/32 -p tcp -m multiport --dports 2022,8090 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# tunnel-probe to office-db-pc's MSSQL (ScheduledReportAggregator's docs/office-database-access.md, 7).
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.21/32 -d 10.8.0.10/32 -p tcp --dport 1433 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# timeclock-dev to the central log server (timeclock design 12, R22).
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.26/32 -d 10.8.0.25/32 -p tcp --dport 9020 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# timeclock-dev to timeclock-backend's database relay (timeclock design 12, R26.1).
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.26/32 -d 10.8.0.24/32 -p tcp --dport 5432 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# timeclock-system-main-office-timeclock to the central log server (timeclock design 12, R22).
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.27/32 -d 10.8.0.25/32 -p tcp --dport 9020 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
# timeclock-system-main-office-timeclock to timeclock-backend's database relay (timeclock design 12, R26.1).
-A FORWARD -i wg0 -o wg0 -s 10.8.0.27/32 -d 10.8.0.24/32 -p tcp --dport 5432 -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -j ACCEPT
COMMIT
